  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n[autofocus-delegate](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#autofocus-delegate) is currently using the DOM tree to find descendants with `autofocus`, although perhaps it should use the flat tree instead.\nFor example, consider\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<dialog id=d>\n  <input placeholder=\"no autofocus\">\n  <div id=host>\n    <template shadowrootmode=open shadowrootdelegatesfocus>\n      <input placeholder=autofocus autofocus>\n    </template>\n  </div>\n</dialog>\n<button autofocus onclick=d.showModal()>click me</button>\n```\nAccording to the spec, the non-autofocus input should be focused when the dialog is opened (Firefox and WebKit do this, but not Chrome), but this is a bit unintuitive.\n\nRelated Gecko bug: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2050985",
